{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1196947-failed-rite-of-passage","id":1196947,"title":"Failed Rite of Passage","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-18T16:38:35-07:00","id":1196947,"title":"Failed Rite of Passage","content":"<div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So this was a post in another thread: (emphasis is mine)</span></span></span></div> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1193048-red-talons-in-packs-with-homid-garou?p=1195270#post1195270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">It would very well be raised by another tribe who has lesser standards towards heritage, Children of Gaia, Bonegnawer, if female Black Fury, if suitable Stargazer.</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><i><b>Only if the cub can't make the Rite of Passage into another tribe, it would be Ronin.</b></i></span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bIt got me thinking. If you have a Garou cub who cannot seem to successfully complete a Rite of Passage, what happens? I disagree with heinrich. I'm not thinking that the cub automatically becomes Ronin (although that's obviously an eventual possibility, especially if the cub gets frustrated or whatever). And of course for some tribes (Get for instance) &quot;fail&quot; is synonymous with &quot;dead&quot;... But say you've got a CoG or a Stargazer cub and no matter how many times they get put through a Rite of Passage, they just fall flat. Can't get the hang of their Auspice -- can't get in tune with the Tribal Totem -- don't get the spirits... whatever. The essential elements of being Garou just don't click for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat happens?</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T17:15:10-07:00","id":1196962,"title":"","content":"If it's a friendly and progressive Tribe, and they have supportive people around them, try a different tribe? Children of Gaia wouldn't want to try and pretend a Ronin was one of them of course, but they could work to try and fit them with another Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T17:44:22-07:00","id":1196973,"title":"","content":"If the cub fails the Rite of Passage for the tribe that claimed him, some tribes might allow him to retake the passage at a later time. Some tribes would not allow a second chance (Silver Fangs and Get of Fenris would be my examples), but others may (like Children of Gaia). For other tribes, it may depend on the particular sept of that tribe. <br /> <br /> Whenever that option is exhausted, the next option would be for the Garou to go to one of the other tribes and petition them to allow the cub to go. So someone who could not pass the Silver Fang rite of passage, might be picked up by any number of tribes who realize a &quot;failed&quot; SF might still be pretty good (I could see Shadow Lords and Fianna, among others, be willing to accept such cubs). For the cubs of other tribes who can't hack it, the tribes that accept them might be very low on the totem pole - like the Bone Gnawers.<br /> <br /> If they still screw up and can't do it, then eeking out an existence as a Ronin would be the default. In practice though, I could see some such cubs experience an early Harano and consciously or subconsciously choose suicide as the only way to handle their shame.<br /> <br /> I believe that while Rites of Passage do test the cubs severely, that I don't think they are all that hard to do. Rites of Passage are meant to signify transition into adulthood. The cub is now ready to take on the responsibilities of an adult. Rites can involve things that are dangerous or hard to master, but they are not meant to purposefully fail. Every tribe will do their best to prepare their cubs to succeed. Some tribes, like the Get of Fenris, do set a higher bar to cross, but that likely comes from practical experience - every Get of Fenris wants to make sure that a future packmate can be relied upon so that not only they do not die, that they do not get their packmates killed either. Likewise the Stargazers need Garou who possess the intellectual rigor that Chimera demands. They can't accept any old idiot who can't figure out enigmas - although I would not be surprised if the Stargazers are also one of the tribes who allow multiple rites of passage to happen since a single failure may not mean the cub can't hack it. And because those high standard tribes are known, &quot;rejects&quot; from them will find homes elsewhere even if the cub is personally humiliated by their failure. So a cub who can't pass ANY rite of passage has to be very rare and very screwed up. In that case, I don't see the tribes accepting them and they end up as ronin. Of course, even they might shape up at some point, do well, and earn a reputation to the point that some tribe would accept them as a graduate of the school of hard knocks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T18:06:22-07:00","id":1196978,"title":"","content":"Okay, assuming that the Garou in question just <i>cannot</i> pass <i>any</i> Rite of Passage (for whatever reason), you are all in agreement that the cub would get kicked out of the tribe? Even the CoGs or Gnawers? Like, the way I'd see it is that if the cub got rejected by their first (or second or third) tribe and eventually wound up getting pawned off on the CoGs -- and <i>still</i> can't pass even the Children's Rite of Passage -- would the CoGs really just kick the cub out on his butt? Like, I could see him becoming a &quot;perpetual cub&quot; who's sort of the butt of every joke and has no standing in the sept. But, &quot;Get out, and try not to get raped by the Black Spirals on the way&quot;? Like, even for the Garou, that seems sort of harsh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T22:57:05-07:00","id":1197050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1196947-failed-rite-of-passage?p=1196978#post1196978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, assuming that the Garou in question just <i>cannot</i> pass <i>any</i> Rite of Passage (for whatever reason), you are all in agreement that the cub would get kicked out of the tribe? Even the CoGs or Gnawers? Like, the way I'd see it is that if the cub got rejected by their first (or second or third) tribe and eventually wound up getting pawned off on the CoGs -- and <i>still</i> can't pass even the Children's Rite of Passage -- would the CoGs really just kick the cub out on his butt? Like, I could see him becoming a &quot;perpetual cub&quot; who's sort of the butt of every joke and has no standing in the sept. But, &quot;Get out, and try not to get raped by the Black Spirals on the way&quot;? Like, even for the Garou, that seems sort of harsh.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It seems like its extremely hard to fail the rite of passage even the more extreme ones where failure means death generally set it up so that things are tipped in the favor of the cubs. They also generally aren't sent off alone so even if one guy is kind of a fuck up if the test succeeds as a group then everyone passes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T04:20:49-07:00","id":1197125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1196947-failed-rite-of-passage?p=1197050#post1197050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems like its extremely hard to fail the rite of passage even the more extreme ones where failure means death generally set it up so that things are tipped in the favor of the cubs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you read the Rite of Passage ( <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Rite_of_Passage_(book\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Rite_of_Passage_(book</a>) ) ?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/562-lachdanan","name":"Lachdanan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar562_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T05:31:12-07:00","id":1197139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lachdanan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1196947-failed-rite-of-passage?p=1197125#post1197125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Have you read the Rite of Passage ( <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Rite_of_Passage_(book\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Rite_of_Passage_(book</a>) ) ?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its all sorts of special, some of the suggested ones seem like &quot;and how does this tribe exist at all?&quot; I mean for fuck's sake some Fera have as their Rite.. &quot;Pick a Bowl&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T08:06:58-07:00","id":1197198,"title":"","content":"We are focusing on homids here, but what about lupus and metis. Would the Nation let a lupus become a ronin if they failed their Rite? What about a metis?<br /> <br /> Plus, there are so many different ways a RoP is seen. Some see it as a group thing, some as a lone thing. Another thing is that some do not have a failure state other than death. It is just up to the cub to solve the situation -someday-","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T09:33:39-07:00","id":1197236,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately it has occurred to many a character and it is indeed severity based on the amount of failure witnessed by the spirits/elders, the tribe outlook itself, it's structure of leadership present, how good the pup can use its social attributes/Pure Breed etc to get another chance in a convincing manner.<br /> <br /> There's a big difference from failing in front of a Rank 3 Wendigo Theurge named Care-of-Bears compared to failing in front of a Rank 6 Ahroun Elder named Scalps-the-Weak and you just happen to be the very pale cousin of Evan-Heals-the-Past. There's a good chance your new name is going to be Fails-to-Live.<br /> <br /> The mature thing to do would be to make the pup wield the Flaw &quot;Probationary Sect Member&quot; until it gets it stuff together. The pup wont so much as even have the right to speak among tribal affairs and may have to stay outside the Caern borders until mentored enough to be summoned for another try. If players argue over it make them draw straws in character. Because if no one stands up on behalf of the failure at all it will be cast out or maybe even killed. In the case of an entire group failing. There may or may not be a Garou who is willing to step in thinking they got what it takes.<br /> <br /> -However.. Get of Fenris would label the cub a &quot;B@T%H&quot; with a very painful &quot;You don't belong here&quot; strapped to it..<br /> <br /> -The Children of Gaia would lean towards nursing the failed pups broken confidence like a child with a skinned knee who fell off a bike in Mr. Rogers Neighborhood.<br /> -Red Talons are quick to hit a failure with &quot;NO ROOM FOR WEAK&quot; which may also indicate it to be killed on sight if it even escapes the angry Master of the Rite while being chased off.<br /> <br /> Every situation is different in its variables.<br /> <br /> And yes I do agree.. That if by some chance of horrific fate the cub is the Charlie Brown of Garou and just can't kick the football even when you glue it on his shoe.. He's cast out. Every elders knows all it takes is one weak link to make the chain pointless. This is natural selection not an audition for the Ewoks cartoon.<br /> <br /> For a Metis it's even worse because they know better having been raised in direct reflection of it's structure.<br /> <br /> It's tragic for a Lupus because it's life structure starting out is feral in nature. The weak do not survive..<br /> <br /> (Edit: ----&gt; C: &lt;---so you can see this smiley face I posted<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23973-silentline","user":"Silentline","date":". 03-19-2018, 12:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23973-silentline","name":"Silentline","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T16:29:22-07:00","id":1197383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silentline</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1196947-failed-rite-of-passage?p=1197236#post1197236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's a big difference from failing in front of a Rank 3 Wendigo Theurge named Care-of-Bears compared to failing in front of a Rank 6 Ahroun Elder named Scalps-the-Weak and you just happen to be the very pale cousin of Evan-Heals-the-Past. There's a good chance your new name is going to be Fails-to-Live.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWish I could hit the &quot;like&quot; button multiple times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Silentline</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1196947-failed-rite-of-passage?p=1197236#post1197236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yes I do agree.. That if by some chance of horrific fate the cub is the Charlie Brown of Garou and just can't kick the football even when you glue it on his shoe.. He's cast out. Every elders knows all it takes is one weak link to make the chain pointless. This is natural selection not an audition for the Ewoks cartoon.</div> </div> </div> </div>There<i> is</i> another side to this however. It doesn't address the matter directly, but on page 35 of the Glass Walkers Tribebook, the various members of Genereader's pack are discussing the pros and cons of making Rites of Passage easier or harder. The following point gets made:<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;There's a lot of debate that flies around how challenging these Rites of Passage should be. On the one hand, we want our soldiers to be of a certain standard. This is a war, not a kindergarten class, and making a Rite of Passage easy for a hopeless case can, actually will, be costly later. On the other hand, any Garou is better than none and throwing a group of cubs to the -- erm -- wolves is a waste of resources. Even the most incompetent, loathsome screw-up can breed, if nothing else.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bNow that's just one member, of one pack, of one tribe -- but I wonder how the other tribes view this little conundrum that there just aren't enough Garou by far (and growing steadily fewer) to just chuck cubs at random. I'm thinking that if you've got a sept that's in such dire straits that they're pushing some of their lesser missions off onto Kinfolk fellowships, that at a minimum the <i>Kin</i> would welcome a Garou who can at a minimum, step sideways and regenerate bullet wounds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T17:49:44-07:00","id":1197407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1196947-failed-rite-of-passage#post1196947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So this was a post in another thread: (emphasis is mine)</span></span></span></div><div align=\"left\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200bIt got me thinking. If you have a Garou cub who cannot seem to successfully complete a Rite of Passage, what happens? I disagree with heinrich. I'm not thinking that the cub automatically becomes Ronin (although that's obviously an eventual possibility, especially if the cub gets frustrated or whatever). And of course for some tribes (Get for instance) &quot;fail&quot; is synonymous with &quot;dead&quot;... But say you've got a CoG or a Stargazer cub and no matter how many times they get put through a Rite of Passage, they just fall flat. Can't get the hang of their Auspice -- can't get in tune with the Tribal Totem -- don't get the spirits... whatever. The essential elements of being Garou just don't click for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat happens?</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If you keep failing a right of passage its a competence issue. Even severely crippled Metis can still often succeed in a right of passage. So if you are so incompetent that you keep failing you are likely going to be shuffled into the Bonegnawers who often have insanely low standards. If you fail there, you may be put down. I mean why are you failing if you actually have tried multiple times? Is it because you are too insane to function? Is your intelligence too low, even the military makes it illegal to accept someone with an IQ of lower then 83. Are you too cowardly? What?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T23:01:14-07:00","id":1197496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1196947-failed-rite-of-passage#post1196947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">So this was a post in another thread: (emphasis is mine)</span></span></span></div> <div align=\"left\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">\u200b And of course for some tribes (Get for instance) &quot;fail&quot; is synonymous with &quot;dead&quot;...<br /> <br /> \u200bWhat happens?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'd agree that the Rite for any Tribe it self might be that dangerous, but assume you meant that the Get execute their failures. I also assume the those that survive the passage within passing it may be shunned by the rest of the Garou community as a lost pup or wolf until the rest of they're days or until such time they can take the test again. Maybe this happens when they put their own life on the line to save other initiate pups from some random catastrophe (That wasn't supposed to happen.) during their own rite of passage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T23:04:25-07:00","id":1197498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1196947-failed-rite-of-passage?p=1197407#post1197407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you keep failing a right of passage its a competence issue. Even severely crippled Metis can still often succeed in a right of passage.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bLike, I'm not really sure I agree with that. The ultimate purpose of the Rite is to ensure that a Garou doesn't make it to Cliath unless they've proven that they're up to the tribal standards (and it's generally held that those standards are supposed to be fairly high). Now once upon a time, the Garou could afford to be really choosy about whom they allowed into the sacred brotherhood of a tribe... In the modern age, not so much. And in the novels, there's some references to some Rites being highly cursory &quot;bullsh** Rites&quot; as a result. But the reason that such Rites of Passage are given such disdain is explicitly because they basically defeat the purpose for the Rite to begin with -- which is to truly test the prospective Garou. If (as you propose) Rites are by their nature so simple and straightforward enough that even crippled Garou can regularly pass them -- then what exactly is the purpose of the Rite?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1196947-failed-rite-of-passage?p=1197407#post1197407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I mean why are you failing if you actually have tried multiple times? Is it because you are too insane to function? Is your intelligence too low, even the military makes it illegal to accept someone with an IQ of lower then 83. Are you too cowardly? What?</div> </div> </div> </div>There could be many reasons. A recurring theme is that with the dispersion of Kin (and the increasing percentage of Lost Cubs as a result), the Garou Nation has issues with cubs going Ronin due to simple culture shock. If a sept needs new Garou too badly to let a pack-to-be get acquainted with each other and their natures and throws them into a Rite before they're ready and they cannot function as a pack because last week they were all hanging out at the mall and have no frame of reference to operating in a militaristic hierarchy. Maybe they're not mentally prepared yet to deal with even the concept of spirits (much less try bargaining with a predator spirit that might try to eat you). Maybe their entire upbringing is in conflict with their new Auspice. These things should not be easy or simple to resolve. And yeah, the really good ones can deal with that sh** on the fly... But I'm talking about people who don't yet have any emotional investment, dedication to cause, or will to combat yet. Ideally, no elder would put such a cub into a Rite on zero notice (much less an entire pack), but this is the World of Darkness we're talking about here.<br /> <br /> \u200bEDIT: Actually, one other thing comes to mind here: In another thread the issue of the disparity of social standing between the Kin and the Garou came up. One argument for why Garou are right in holding themselves so far above their Kin, and why it would be proper for Kin to be excluded from having some fairly basic rights and privileges is that the Garou are held to such a high standard that no Kin could possibly compare. Specifically, that no Kin could possibly pass a meaningful Rite of Passage -- but now apparently the Rite is this super-easy thing that only the werewolf equivalent to Rain Man would possibly fail. Just saying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":3506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","user":"Uniform Two Six","date":". 03-20-2018, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T02:20:04-07:00","id":1197523,"title":"","content":"I think it's worth remembering that the Rite of Passage is customized for each instance. Cubs rarely go into the quest alone, and the quests are tailored to the cubs. A Fenrir ritemaster is going to set different parameters for two Ragabash and a Theurge than they would for three Ahrouns, even if both instances are going to involve killing some Wyrm thing. The Fianna might purposefully screw Metis over by making sure their deformities are a hindrance to the quest, while the Fenrir might set it up more as a chance to prove the Metis' deformity isn't going to stop them, while the Gnawers might avoid anything that would highlight a deformity at all.<br /> <br /> That flexibility means that opinions on any given instance of the Rite can vary with some Gaoru considering it a cake-walk, and others a proper challenge, and others something too harsh. The Garou aren't exactly unified. But the Rite only works if the Totems OK it, so any Garou - however begrudgingly - has to take a Cliath as a Cliath if the Rite worked (as they have to do for any other increases in Rank). There's a PC in a game I'm in that basically didn't even have a Rite of Passage (their challenge was, &quot;go tell the Sept's Cubs how you managed to get here,&quot;) because their life as a Lost Cub was harsh enough that the Gnawers didn't think the character's mettle needed even more testing.<br /> <br /> It's also how failing Rites of Passage (esp. multiple times) can be seen as exceedingly rare, even if most Garou's quests are tough enough that their first Rank feels earned.<br /> <br /> A character that simply can't pass the Rite ever is so bad at this, that despite the challenge being custom tailored to their strengths and weaknesses, they always choke. It's so rare I'm not sure it's worth considering. Those poor souls are not filling out the Ranks of the BSDs or Ronin","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T02:33:27-07:00","id":1197529,"title":"","content":"The 'Rite of Passage' books examples for Rites of Passage per tribe are somewhat outdated with the way the Setting has developed. That aside, I didn't want to imply that one failing a Rite of Passage is automatically a Ronin. I would guess that they would loose Renown, so they might need additional time and training to get the Cliath starting Renown, but if they have, they might get another try at a Rite of Passage.<br /> <br /> It is those cubs who the septs loose faith in or those cubs who loose faith in themselves and therefore opt out of the Garou Nation and the Tribe who become Ronin. That is, if the Tribe/Sept permits them to live. In Outcasts the Ronin explains that to petition access to a caern from a sept, one must do something usually, and that doing something shady for the Shadow Lords is still better than listening to some Children of Gaia Elders for hours, while they try to convince you to come back into the fold. So, being Ronin isn't a no return thing. But, even the Bone Gnawers have standards and customs and a way of life you must understand and embrace, if you want to be one of them, which beats being Ronin usually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T02:35:17-07:00","id":1197530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1196947-failed-rite-of-passage?p=1197523#post1197523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's worth remembering that the Rite of Passage is customized for each instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly. It certainly is, when we play one in LARP. But, the 1st Edition Children of Gaia tribe book is basically a Rite of Passage - the cub telling the Elders all there is to know about the tribe as a means of exam. It might be the go-to Rite of Passage in this sept.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-20T10:02:38-07:00","id":1197656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1196947-failed-rite-of-passage?p=1197383#post1197383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bWish I could hit the &quot;like&quot; button multiple times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Silentline -&quot;WOOT! XD LOL&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1196947-failed-rite-of-passage?p=1197383#post1197383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There<i> is</i> another side to this however. It doesn't address the matter directly, but on page 35 of the Glass Walkers Tribebook, the various members of Genereader's pack are discussing the pros and cons of making Rites of Passage easier or harder. The following point gets made:<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;There's a lot of debate that flies around how challenging these Rites of Passage should be. On the one hand, we want our soldiers to be of a certain standard. This is a war, not a kindergarten class, and making a Rite of Passage easy for a hopeless case can, actually will, be costly later. On the other hand, any Garou is better than none and throwing a group of cubs to the -- erm -- wolves is a waste of resources. Even the most incompetent, loathsome screw-up can breed, if nothing else.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bNow that's just one member, of one pack, of one tribe -- but I wonder how the other tribes view this little conundrum that there just aren't enough Garou by far (and growing steadily fewer) to just chuck cubs at random. I'm thinking that if you've got a sept that's in such dire straits that they're pushing some of their lesser missions off onto Kinfolk fellowships, that at a minimum the <i>Kin</i> would welcome a Garou who can at a minimum, step sideways and regenerate bullet wounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Silentline- &quot;Very True indeed in all respects. The failure of a Rite of passage is sometimes a good thing.. As each tribe has its main point as indicated by each Tribal Lore rating level explaining what the tribe truly stands for and why. The Bone Gnawer tribal lore within the Bone Gnawer Tribe book is interesting however the Children of Gaia Tribal lore at rank five is incredibly interesting and downright depressing to a certain degree. So failed rites make makes sense on some occasions as the pup may be out of sync with the tribal focus.. The unseen hand guiding a traveler to its true destination so to speak.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23973,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23973-silentline","user":"Silentline","date":". 03-20-2018, 01:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23973-silentline","name":"Silentline","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T09:27:46-07:00","id":1201297,"title":"","content":"I dont see them sitting idly by if a nest of formori The Cubs were sent to clean out wind up having a pack of Dancers in control I see the grown ups moving in, but the Rite would have to be repeated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T18:01:15-07:00","id":1201490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uniform Two Six</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1196947-failed-rite-of-passage?p=1197383#post1197383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...page 35 of the Glass Walkers Tribebook...<br /> <br /> \u200b&quot;There's a lot of debate that flies around how challenging these Rites of Passage should be. On the one hand, we want our soldiers to be of a certain standard. This is a war, not a kindergarten class, and making a Rite of Passage easy for a hopeless case can, actually will, be costly later. On the other hand, any Garou is better than none and throwing a group of cubs to the -- erm -- wolves is a waste of resources. Even the most incompetent, loathsome screw-up can breed, if nothing else.&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200bNow that's just one member, of one pack, of one tribe -- but I wonder how the other tribes view this little conundrum that there just aren't enough Garou by far (and growing steadily fewer) to just chuck cubs at random. I'm thinking that if you've got a sept that's in such dire straits that they're pushing some of their lesser missions off onto Kinfolk fellowships, that at a minimum the <i>Kin</i> would welcome a Garou who can at a minimum, step sideways and regenerate bullet wounds.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd agree with the opinion expressed by that Glass Walker. Garou lives are a precious resource that shouldn't be thrown away but rarely. If a cub fails his or her rite of passage more than once, it's still worth the effort to keep the cub around, if for no other reason than as a breeder -- especially if the cub is a lupus -- but probably also because there's hope the cub eventually might grow up. Passing for Cliath at age 30 probably means you'll never amount to much in the Garou Nation, but it's better than if the tribe killed you when you failed the first time at age 20. If the cub is so weak or incompetent that no role at all can be found for him or her, one last attempt should be given where failure = death. Even if the cub fails and dies, it's more honorable, and more merciful, than being killed by the sept or exiled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-31T06:00:19-07:00","id":1201591,"title":"","content":"think I was right grown ups will be ready if it seems to be too much of a challenge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}